                <td width=572 valign=center colspan=10 style="width:343.6000pt;padding:0.0000pt 5.4000pt 0.0000pt 5.4000pt ;border-left:none;
mso-border-left-alt:none;border-right:1.0000pt solid windowtext;mso-border-right-alt:0.5000pt solid windowtext;
border-top:none;mso-border-top-alt:0.5000pt solid windowtext;border-bottom:1.0000pt solid windowtext;
mso-border-bottom-alt:0.5000pt solid windowtext;">
                    <p class=MsoNormal><span style="font-family:仿宋;mso-bidi-font-family:'Times New Roman';font-size:12.0000pt;
mso-font-kerning:1.0000pt;"><font face="仿宋"><p><strong>Introduction to Geriatrics of Traditional Chinese Medicine</strong>&nbsp;is a clinical discipline that applies TCM theories and methods to study the etiology, pathomechanisms, diagnosis, treatment principles, prevention, and management of diseases in the elderly. The course is structured into a general overview of TCM geriatrics and specific discussions on common diseases affecting various organ systems in older adults. It emphasizes the distinctive features of geriatric medicine and highlights TCM clinical reasoning, while also incorporating updated knowledge from integrative Chinese-Western geriatric medicine to enhance the educational content.</p>
<p>Traditional Chinese Medicine is grounded in a profound humanistic heritage. Its origins and evolution are deeply intertwined with humanities disciplines such as philosophy, astronomy, history, and literature. By integrating TCM’s cultural framework with its academic model, the subject is taught and studied through its cultural dimensions.</p></font></span><span style="font-family:'Times New Roman';mso-fareast-font-family:仿宋;font-size:10.5000pt;
mso-font-kerning:1.0000pt;"><o:p></o:p></span></p>
                </td>
            </tr>
